3. VERSION HISTORY

v2.0 (10-Nov-2026)
  * inflate() takes the input length and the output capacity and
    reports truncated input, bad codes, bad distances and a size that
    does not match the header. Lengths are int.
  * The Nintendo DS entry point is inflate_ds.c in this directory.
    The separate inflateTT-DS tree is gone.
  * The makefile builds inflate.o and inflate_ds.o.

v1.3 (25-Nov-2007)
  * The header file is now C++ compatible.
  * Added return values to inflate().
  * Encapsulated all the variables inflate() require into an inflateContext
    structure thus making inflate() thread safe.

v1.2 (06-May-2007)
  * Added support for deflateTT v1.2 (DEFc) files.

v1.1 (21-Apr-2007)
  * The Huffman codes aren't read from the compressed files,
    but generated from the code lengths making this more
    RFC-1951 compatible.

v1.0 (27-Jan-2007)
  * The first public release


